From: PLANK Engineering <engineering@instinctual.la>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/videotoolbox: require hardware for HEVC

PLANK HEVC sessions require hardware decoding. Merely enabling acceleration
allows VideoToolbox to return a software decoder that still uses CVPixelBuffers.
Keep ProRes behavior unchanged; H.264 already requires hardware in this backend
and may fall back to the independent FFmpeg software decoder in the Client.

--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
@@ -845,8 +845,7 @@ static CFDictionaryRef videotoolbox_decoder_config_create(CMVideoCodecType codec_type,
                                                                    &kCFTypeDictionaryValueCallBacks);
 
     CFDictionarySetValue(config_info,
-                        avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC
-                        || avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_PRORES
+                        avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_PRORES
                         || avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_PRORES_RAW
                             ?
                             kVTVideoDecoderSpecification_EnableHardwareAcceleratedVideoDecoder :
